        "original_id": "cfe2d27d-b767-539f-a676-78ee349f40eb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mikhail Vasilyevich Lomonosov\n- Products: Akademik Lomonosov\n- Roles: Academician, polymath, scientist, writer\n- Concepts: atmosphere of Venus, Law of Mass Conservation, chemical reactions\n- Topics: literature, education, natural science, chemistry, physics, mineralogy, history, art, philology, optical devices\n\nFacts:\n- Mikhail Vasilyevich Lomonosov was born on November 19, 1711, and died on April 15, 1765.\n- Mikhail Vasilyevich Lomonosov was a Russian polymath, scientist, and writer.\n- Mikhail Vasilyevich Lomonosov made important contributions to literature, education, and science.\n- Mikhail Vasilyevich Lomonosov discovered the atmosphere of Venus and the Law of Mass Conservation in chemical reactions.\n- Mikhail Vasilyevich Lomonosov worked in natural science, chemistry, physics, mineralogy, history, art, philology, and optical devices.\n- The ship Akademik Lomonosov was named after Academician Mikhail Lomonosov.",
